From 393f78a0bd5878d84f043e9a71c7a8e2dca77c26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:17:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Q4 prefill: query-tiled MiniMax-M3 sparse attention for
 prefill-sized calls

vLLM's _gqa_sparse_fwd_kernel runs one program per (query token, kv head) and loads that
token's 16 selected 128-token KV blocks, so each block is re-read from L2 by every token
that picked it. Real indexer selections are strongly correlated between neighbours: an
8-token tile's union averages 18.9 blocks against 128 unshared (captured live topk_idx).

sparse_attn_tiled.py takes 8 consecutive rows of one request per program, iterates the
sorted union of their selected blocks once, and masks per row (selection, causal, seq
length) so every row attends exactly its own blocks; only the order in which blocks enter
the online softmax differs. Against an fp32 reference it matches vLLM's kernel to three
digits (1.5-2.3e-3, tests/gpu/test_sparse_attn_tiled.py); per call 12.4 -> 5.6 ms.

The q4 prefill wrapper uses it for calls with >= VLLM_EXL3_SPARSE_TILED_MIN_ROWS rows (1024)
and keeps vLLM's kernel below that (short prompts, the NLL-check passages);
VLLM_EXL3_SPARSE_TILED=0 disables it. Served prefill 8K/16K 1167/1221 -> 1237/1268 tok/s.
